// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    The Lancer
// @category Characterization / Relationships
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/The_Lancer
// @domain   Interpersonal
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): the lieutenant and Foil for The Hero — the second-in-command, usually a
// contrast to the lead (clean-cut hero -> grizzled snarker; driven hero -> relaxed and level-headed),
// yet a grouchy-but-loyal Number Two. FRONTIER: the Lancer is the SUM of two corpus dyads — it is The
// Foil (contrast on a shared axis) AND a loyal second-in-command at once. Neither alone is a Lancer:
// a pure foil need not be loyal or subordinate; a pure sidekick need not contrast. The capability is
// recognizing the conjunction — loyalty ACROSS a difference — that defines the number two who both
// completes and challenges the number one.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/concepts/index.trl"            // loyalty, contrast, identity

assoc the_lancer -> [
  the_foil     : "is a loyal, subordinate kind of",
  the_sidekick : "is the contrasting, second-in-command kind of",
  loyalty      : "holds across a difference, which is the heart of",
  contrast     : "is defined, like the foil, by"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===

imply Lancer -> [Foil, loyalty, Contrast, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// The capability: a SECOND who foils the hero on a shared axis (opposite value) AND stays loyally
// subordinate to them. The conjunction is the whole point — the contrast is the foil half, the
// Seconds bond is the sidekick half, and the Lancer is the one character carrying both. This is
// strictly narrower than rule Foil (which needs no loyalty) and rule The_Sidekick (which needs no
// contrast).
rule The_Lancer {
  when:
    char $h [+Protagonist]
    char $l [@Foils(other=$h)] [@Seconds(leader=$h)]
    char $h [+Trait(axis=$d, value=$vh)]
    char $l [+Trait(axis=$d, value=$vl)]
    $vh != $vl
  then:
    $l [+Lancer]
    $l [+Illuminated(by=$h)]
    $h [+Illuminated(by=$l)]
    $h [+Challenged(by=$l)]
    $l -- contrast
    $l -- loyalty
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: Star Wars — Han Solo to Luke Skywalker (film, 1977) ===
// Same axis as the farmboy — what to believe in — but opposite value: Luke is all faith (the Force,
// the cause); Han is all cynicism ("hokey religions and ancient weapons are no match for a good
// blaster"). The smuggler comes back for the trench run anyway. He foils the hero's idealism and is
// his loyal second — that conjunction, loyalty across the difference, is the Lancer.

// LUKE SKYWALKER
char luke [+Protagonist] [+Courageous] [+Trait(axis=conviction, value=faith)]

// HAN SOLO
char han  [+Deuteragonist] [+Loyal] [+Trait(axis=conviction, value=cynicism)]
han [@Foils(other=luke)] [@Seconds(leader=luke)]

scene the_trench_run {
  beat 1 {
    han -- luke : "you're all clear, kid — now blow this thing and go home"
    // The_Lancer -> han [+Lancer] [+Illuminated(by=luke)], luke [+Challenged(by=han)]
  }
}
